    "question": {
      ":question/id": "4fe4ab34-9f13-5b51-bf31-d28429a312aa",
      ":question/problem": "Find the determinant of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -3 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\nUse a Laplace expansion along row 3, then evaluate the triangular minor.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Write $D=\\det(A)$.\n\nExpand $D$ along row 3; only 1 nonzero entry contributes.\n\n$$\nD=(-3)(-1)^{3+1}\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWrite $D_{1}$ for the minor obtained by deleting row 3 and column 1.\n\nThe matrix in $D_{1}$ is triangular, so multiply its diagonal entries.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D_{1} &=\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ &=(-3)\\cdot(1)\\cdot(3) \\\\ &=-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these minor values,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D &=(-3)(-1)^{3+1}(-9) \\\\ &=27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\det(A)=27$.",
